    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16084" root="رفأ" body-key="r">
    
      2 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رفّآهُ</span></b> , (T, S, M, K,) inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَرْفِئَةٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَرْفِىْءٌ</span>,
(T, S, K,) <i>He said to him,</i> (namely, a man who
had had a wife given to him, T, S, M,) <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بِالرِّفَآءِ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَالبَنِينَ</span>; (T, S, M, K; [see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رِفَآءٌ</span>, below;]) as also
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رفّاهُ</span>, without <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ء</span>. (TA.)

